<title>CANADA: Kinross acquires Falconbridge land.</title>
<headline>Kinross acquires Falconbridge land.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kinross Gold Corp said Thursday it has exercised its option with Falconbridge Ltd to buy a number of Canadian gold properties for C$1.9 million.</p>
<p>Under a June 1994 deal between Kinross and Pentland Firth Ventures Ltd, Pentland paid Kinross C$400,000 as its share of the exercise of the Falconbridge option, Kinross said in a statement.</p>
<p>As a result, Kinross has acquired one property in Ontario, just east of its Hoyle Pond mine, and a number of properties in Quebec, the company said.</p>
<p>Pentland has acquired 16 properties in Ontario.  </p>
<p>Kinross has a 49 percent interest in Pentland.</p>
<p>Kinross said it has recently opened an office in Val d'Or, Quebec, to guide exploration of the properties. Some of them will likely be optioned to other interested companies, it said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
